### ⚙️ Offline Functionality
Suggestions:

- IndexedDB or Local Storage: Store simulations and notes locally for offline access.
- "Downloaded Content" Page: Allow students to pre-download selected chapters or quizzes.

### 🌐 UI/UX Enhancements
Suggestions:

- Dark Mode Toggle
- Bookmarking Topics
- Search by Formula or Law: A student can search “F = ma” and land on Newton’s Second Law content.
- Sticky Sidebar: Keep the sidebar fixed on scroll so that students can quickly switch sections while reading long content or quizzes.
- Use Real Graphics Instead of 600x400 Placeholders: Add subject-relevant images or illustrations for Simulations, Study Materials, and Quizzes. Use platforms like https://undraw.co or https://icons8.com for free SVGs.
- Add Titles to Cards (Not Just Buttons): Each card should have a bold, clear title (e.g., “Interactive Simulations”) on top, and your button can say something more specific like “Start Simulating”, “View Notes”, “Take a Quiz”.
- Homepage Welcome Section - Text Readability: Split the intro into two lines with emphasis.
- Homepage Welcome Section - Call to Action (CTA): Add one bold button like 🚀 Start Learning Now! or Browse Topics →.
- 📱 Responsive Design: Make sure the sidebar collapses into a hamburger menu on mobile and stack the content cards vertically on small screens.
- Change “Explore” to something more action-driven like: "Open", "Learn", "Try Now", or icon + text (📘 Explore).
- Guest User Indicator: In bottom-left, "Guest — Not Logged In" is fine, but add a subtle “Login for full access” tooltip or indicator.

